[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3190965382","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109616#issuecomment-3190965382","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109616","id":3190965382,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-MkSG","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-15T08:42:36Z","updated_at":"2025-08-15T08:42:36Z","body":"As mentioned on [the contributors chat](https://chat.godotengine.org/channel/buildsystem?msg=bWmkvbai5aPrc9fuB), that CI run of `Test Godot project` with ThreadSanitizer enabled resulted in around 40 reports of various race conditions, but for some reason the test is still considered to have run successfully. ThreadSanitizer is supposed to set the exit code to 66 when something has been reported.\r\n\r\nIt could be that `TSAN_OPTIONS=halt_on_error=1` is needed. It seems like a good thing to set either way. If you look at the timestamps in the logs you'll see that it spent roughly 13 minutes just reporting those ThreadSanitizer warnings, which I suspect is due to the time spent symbolicating all the stack traces.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3190965382/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3192081128","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109616#issuecomment-3192081128","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109616","id":3192081128,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-Q0ro","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-15T16:23:29Z","updated_at":"2025-08-15T16:23:29Z","body":"Looks like `halt_on_error` is an option multiple sanitizers can use; will try applying that and seeing what comes up","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3192081128/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3192289230","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109616#issuecomment-3192289230","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109616","id":3192289230,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-RnfO","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-15T17:43:59Z","updated_at":"2025-08-15T17:44:18Z","body":"It looks like that did the trick, and apparently surfaced some UBSan errors in one of the other tests as well.\r\n\r\nLooking at past logs for that `Linux / Editor with doubles and GCC sanitizers` job, it looks like we have quite a few UBSan errors that have gone unnoticed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3192289230/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3192318235","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109616#issuecomment-3192318235","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109616","id":3192318235,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-Rukb","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-15T17:58:45Z","updated_at":"2025-08-15T17:58:45Z","body":"That certainly fixed the issue of not getting an error, but I'm not 100% sure if that's the ideal solution. I mean, it's obviously good that a non-zero exit code is now properly returned, but I wonder if that can be accomplished *without* the early exit","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3192318235/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3192356911","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109616#issuecomment-3192356911","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109616","id":3192356911,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-R4Av","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-15T18:15:13Z","updated_at":"2025-08-15T18:15:13Z","body":"Would we actually want it to continue though, especially if it's as slow as it seems to be with printing these reports?\r\n\r\nNote that you can also pass a suppression file using `TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=some_file.txt`. For whatever reason I can't find up-to-date docs for the TSan suppression format, but as best I can tell it hasn't changed all that much from [this](https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/ThreadSanitizerSuppressions) old documentation. You'll likely want `print_suppressions=1` then as well, which will make it print all the matched suppressions at the end.\r\n\r\nUBSan does [actually document](https://clang.llvm.org/docs/UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.html#issue-suppression) their suppression format though. Although that documentation makes it sound like these runtime suppressions don't always work for some reason.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3192356911/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3192565938","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109616#issuecomment-3192565938","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109616","id":3192565938,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-SrCy","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-15T19:51:32Z","updated_at":"2025-08-15T19:51:32Z","body":"We actually do have some suppression files on the repo, but they don't seem to have been updated in a while\r\n\r\nMore pertinently, I've realized why error codes are inconsistent. It comes down to:\r\n1. The CI checking action ignoring Godot's exit code status (???)\r\n2. Running tests will override whatever exit code a sanitizer would've output","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3192565938/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com